From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Priestley <voicedrew11@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:41:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] gs: opt-in recorder of raster backend calls
 (PS2X_GS_RECORD)

PS2X_GS_RECORD=<file> wraps the main GS backend in a decorator that logs
every call (initial VRAM, primitives with their FP rounding mode, CLUT
loads, transfers and upload data, flushes, syncs, presentation requests)
to a binary file. Replaying the file through two backends and comparing
VRAM at the sync points is a deterministic regression test for renderer
changes, independent of guest timing; it also allows profiling the
rasterizer in isolation.
---
 ps2xRuntime/CMakeLists.txt             |   1 +
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_frontend.cpp |   5 +-
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_record.cpp   | 186 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_record.h     |  40 ++++++
 4 files changed, 230 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_record.cpp
 create mode 100644 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_record.h

